        explanation: "Let Principal be P. Sum becomes 2P in 5 years, so Simple Interest (SI) gained = P. Rate of Interest R = (SI * 100)/(P * T) = (P * 100)/(P * 5) = 20% per annum. To become 4 times (4P), SI must be 3P. Time T = (SI * 100)/(P * R) = (3P * 100)/(P * 20) = 15 years. Option C is correct."
